{% doc %}
  The page a page's crumb leads back to (DS-80, DS-184): the handle of the page its eyebrow names
  ("Artists in Residence" names artists-in-residence), or nothing when the eyebrow is blank, names
  no page, or names the page itself. The page header shows the crumb (gs-page-hero, by the same
  rule); the structured data says the same (gs-data, gs-data-page).

  @example
  {%- capture back_handle -%}{% render 'gs-page-back' %}{%- endcapture -%}
  {%- assign back = pages[back_handle] -%}
{% enddoc %}
{%- liquid
  assign eyebrow = page.metafields.custom.eyebrow.value | strip
  if eyebrow != blank
    assign handle = eyebrow | handleize
    assign back = pages[handle]
    if back.id != blank and back.id != page.id
      echo handle
    endif
  endif
-%}
